tps://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d8b146e43c77c50a74ab8967d87b5abd?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-11T17:19:23.000Z"},{"id":"klnoIaJ7z","title":"From Punched Cards to Prompts","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/from-punched-cards-to-prompts/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/from-punched-cards-to-prompts-klnoiaj7z","summary":"Studio Bot has a virtual expert on demand to write, analyze and explain code. Studio Bot doesn\u2019t suggest to separate the `EyeSeU\u2019s declaration from its implementation. It appears that Studio Bot wants to stay within the context of C++ and Assembly Language development.","image":"https://bignerdranch.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/shutterstock_1928496233-2000x1100.png","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-07T19:24:44.000Z"},{"id":"rYc7zMvk9","title":"Big Nerd Ranch and blended learning: why?","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/bnr-and-blended-learning/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/big-nerd-ranch-and-blended-learning-why--ryc7zmvk9","summary":"Big Nerd Ranch is offering its SwiftUI course as a blended learning experience. Students learn best when they have dedicated time and space for learning. Students need to interact with a topic in multiple ways to most effectively learn it. Students can learn more, more quickly when we take away distractions and focus them on learning.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/133ca61945d24869acdca9213ba4e7db?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-06T16:53:41.000Z"},{"id":"SueMNJwYX","title":"Why foray into machine learning?","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/why-foray-into-machine-learning/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-foray-into-machine-learning--suemnjwyx","summary":"Big Nerd Ranch was the first to have a comprehensive method for teaching Mac programming, iOS programming, and Android programming. It was able to train digital staff from across the spectrum, showing them what was possible with this new technology and giving them the confidence to build and explore more. The course was designed to demistify machine learning.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff3cf142b53c3da7a2563b8c9919529f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-24T20:23:09.000Z"},{"id":"B4fFVuzXL","title":"Now Available React Programming: The Big Nerd Ranch Guide","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/react-programming-the-big-nerd-ranch-guide/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/now-available-react-programming-the-big-nerd-ranch-guide-b4ffvuzxl","summary":"The Big Nerd Ranch Guide is based on our React Essentials course. It will help you build a starter app and a complete, production-ready app. You will learn how and when to use the most common React hooks. You will also learn how to test your React components and flows.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/701cb37e953210e3bea7e8d2e06707f1","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-02T21:07:22.000Z"},{"id":"kpfN2j6oP","title":"Asynchronously load images with customized AsyncImage view in SwiftUI","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/asynchronously-load-images-with-customized-asyncimage-view-in-swiftui/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/asynchronously-load-images-with-customized-asyncimage-view-in-swiftui-kpfn2j6op","summary":"Learn how to use AsyncImage in SwiftUI to asynchronously load and display images from a remote URL. Understand the basics of AsyncImage, why you might need a custom version, and how to handle different sources of images.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/854cfeb9124907ab0790eb24ac2aab4b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-27T20:29:22.000Z"},{"id":"eVfaWrxRI","title":"Replacing Myself: Writing Unit Tests with ChatGPT","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/replacing-myself-writing-unit-tests-with-chatgpt/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/replacing-myself-writing-unit-tests-with-chatgpt-evfawrxri","summary":"This post explores the use of ChatGPT in writing unit tests, starting with testing a recursive function and moving on to testing a React reducer and React component. The AI-powered chatbot, ChatGPT, generates unit tests for the provided code, but it also has limitations, such as a lack of creativity, reliance on training data, and the need for human correction. While AI has the potential to revolutionize the way we work, it is not yet ready to replace humans.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/43fab1a1f6b171f1a76a370cc38b9814?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":52,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-04-20T17:53:46.000Z"},{"id":"7EyXNxd9y","title":"The Definition of Done","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/the-definition-of-done/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-definition-of-done-7eyxnxd9y","summary":"The Definition of Done is a checklist of necessary activities for the quality of a feature. It ensures a common understanding among all stakeholders throughout the project. The phases of feature stories are: ready to estimate, ready to play, in development, ready to test, in test (QA), and done.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f4f3ce3f75646fda1c8eeefd763c4d0b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-11T14:00:13.000Z"},{"id":"NK0EOxRJ6","title":"Technical Writing 101: Working with SMEs","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/technical-writing-101-working-with-smes/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/technical-writing-101-working-with-smes-nk0eoxrj6","summary":"Learn about the importance of working with Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) in technical writing and how to collaborate effectively with them.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/63dc61ca85e5c39d09bc239daf55b25e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-06T20:23:54.000Z"},{"id":"q9Dch438q","title":"Using the Navigation Component in Jetpack Compose","url":"https://bignerdranch.com/blog/using-the-navigation-component-in-jetpack-compose/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-the-navigation-component-in-jetpack-compose-q9dch438q","summary":"Jetpack Compose is a declarative framework for building native Android UI. The Navigation Component in Jetpack Compose provides an API for interacting with the Navigation Component, including handling navigation and deep links. However, the lack of argument type safety, repetitive API for passing arguments, and lack of a navigation editor are some of the drawbacks of using the Navigation Component.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/08b1f4150a60e81ed461fcdd627b1655?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-30T18:46:54.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["thatdot","getambassador","beambloggers","fgiesen","codeburst"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"thatdot","handle":"thatdot","name":"thatDot","is_squad":false,"x":0.5943,"y":0.0864,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":65,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e1b0dfcda2d84af09c522096cb78e212","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.640309,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.015385,"avg_read_time":4.630769,"tag_diversity":0.753846},"top_tags_preview":[["machine-learning",10],["architecture",10],["kafka",9]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-6.6029,-7.1029],"cadence_depth":[-2.6176,-3.3088],"hype_variety":[3.5,4.3088],"title_style":[5.2353,6.7647]}},{"id":"getambassador","handle":"getambassador","name":"Ambassador Labs","is_squad":false,"x":0.5523,"y":-0.1116,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":20,"image":"https://media